If I want to run a job from a Docker container, can we do that?

Answer:
Yes, you can run Jenkins jobs within Docker containers using the Docker Pipeline plugin. You define the container in the Jenkins Pipeline script:
groovy
Copy code
pipeline {
    agent {
        docker {
            image 'maven:3.6.3-jdk-8'
            args '-v /root/.m2:/root/.m2'
        }
    }
    stages {
        stage('Build') {
            steps {
                sh 'mvn clean install'
            }
        }
    }
}
