Explain about branching, merging, and branch review strategy that you have used in Git repository?

Answer:
Branching Strategy: We use the Git Flow branching model, which includes feature branches, develop branch, and master branch.
Merging Strategy: Feature branches are merged into the develop branch using pull requests. After thorough code reviews and passing CI tests, develop is merged into the master branch for releases.
Branch Review Strategy: Code reviews are conducted through pull requests. At least one or two team members review the code, ensuring it meets coding standards and passes all tests before merging.
